{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 24, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 american biographical drama film written by aaron sorkin and directed by david fincher. the film is based on the true story of the founding of mark Zuckerberg's social networking site facebook.\n\nthe film follows the story of mark zuckerberg, a brilliant and reclusive college student at harvard university, as he creates a website that eventually becomes facebook. the film explores the complexities of zuckerberg's relationships with his friends and fellow students, including eduardo saverin, andrew mccollum, and sean parker.\n\nthe film features an ensemble cast, including jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, andarmenio barrientos as sean parker. the performances in the film are exceptional, particularly from jesse eisenberg, who brings a depth and nuance to the character of mark zuckerberg.\n\nthe film's direction by david fincher is also noteworthy, as he uses a muted color palette and a fast-paced editing style to convey the sense of chaos and intensity that surrounds zuckerberg's life.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is its script, written by aaron sorkin. sorkin's script is witty and insightful, capturing the complexities and nuances of the characters and their relationships. the dialogue is fast-paced and clever, and sorkin's script is full of clever one-liners and humorous moments.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy. the score is minimalist and atmospheric, perfectly capturing the mood and tone of the film.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that explores the complexities and nuances of the tech industry. the film's performances, direction, and script are all exceptional, making it a must-see for anyone interested in technology, business, or biography.\n\nthe film has received widespread critical acclaim, with many praising its performances, script, and direction. the film has a 96% approval rating on rotten tomatoes, and has won several awards, including the academy award for best original screenplay.\n\nin conclusion, the social network is a film that is both entertaining and thought-provoking. it is a must-see for anyone interested in technology, business, or biography, and is a testament to the power of storytelling and the impact that a single idea can have on the world.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.20552276074886322}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.00030310326837934554}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.04680052399635315}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0009606037638150156}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.5348334312438965}, {"token": "201", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " american", "logprob": -0.2830283045768738}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -0.014159570448100567}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -2.2053474822314456e-05}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.00047052756417542696}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.00013386306818574667}, {"token": " written", "logprob": -2.421853542327881}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.27569782733917236}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.9083265066146851}, {"token": "aron", "logprob": -0.0007084482349455357}, {"token": " s", "logprob": -0.0011689979583024979}, {"token": "ork", "logprob": -9.357491217087954e-05}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.09400942921638489}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -3.981510963058099e-05}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -0.0815265104174614}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -2.95634672511369e-05}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": -0.15473197400569916}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.006627839058637619}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.005301583092659712}, {"token"